IMPORT prelude

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Qld) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts in days ("within 14 days after the day", s 224; "within 30 days after the day",
-- s 229B; "within 14 days after the application ... is received", s 226), in months ("at least 6 months but not more than
-- 18 months since", s 231(1B); "within 3 months after", s 231(2); "within 1 month", s 231(3), (4); "within 6 months
-- after", s 232(1)(c)) and in years ("not more than 1 year after the date", s 113; "within 2 years after", "within 1
-- year after", s 232(1); "at least 5 years from the day", s 38(7)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Work Health and Safety Act 2011`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- "within n days after the day": the day itself is left out, so the period ends n days later.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later day of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `falls after` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier day of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `falls before` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month n months later. A period of n months "after" or "since" a day leaves that day out, so it
-- ends on this day; where the later month is shorter (31 August plus 6 months), the last day of that month (fork F1 in
-- NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the number of days in month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`)) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the start` PLUS n
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS FLOOR ((`the months counted` MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the target month` MEANS ((`the months counted` MINUS 1) MODULO 12) PLUS 1

-- The same day n years later; 29 February falls on 28 February in a year that has none (fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `years after` `the start` MEANS `the day` (n TIMES 12) `months after` `the start`
